      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I'll write the improved test with better understandability — descriptive variable names, a `@DisplayName`, and removing unused imports.Let me check the compile script and working directory structure.The compile script expects the file in the working directory (`testEncodeIgnoreTrimmable/`). I'll write the file there.The improved test compiles successfully. The changes made for better understandability:\n\n1. **Removed unused imports** (`assertNull`, `assertThrows`) that cluttered the original.\n2. **Added `@DisplayName`** to make the test's intent immediately clear without reading the method body.\n3. **Extracted named variables** (`inputWithSurroundingWhitespace`, `expectedSoundexCode`) so the assertion reads as \"expected code equals encoded whitespace-padded input\" rather than a raw string comparison.\n4. **Added a brief comment** explaining that whitespace-surrounded input should produce the same code as the bare word — the non-obvious \"why\" of the test."
